WEBVTT

1
00:00:19,019 --> 00:00:20,287
(beep)

2
00:00:22,489 --> 00:00:25,660
(dramatic music)

3
00:00:48,616 --> 00:00:51,451
(TV buzzing)

4
00:00:54,054 --> 00:00:57,525
(soft piano music)

5
00:01:16,143 --> 00:01:19,681
(soft piano music)

6
00:01:32,292 --> 00:01:33,628
♪ Good morning ♪

7
00:01:33,728 --> 00:01:34,494
(door creaking)

8
00:01:34,596 --> 00:01:36,096
♪ Good morning ♪

9
00:01:36,196 --> 00:01:40,568
♪ I am looking for a pal ♪

10
00:01:40,668 --> 00:01:44,806
♪ Will you pretty
please be my pal ♪

11
00:01:44,906 --> 00:01:48,475
♪ Pretty please, pretty please ♪

12
00:01:48,576 --> 00:01:52,046
♪ Good morning, my good pal ♪

13
00:01:52,145 --> 00:01:57,250
♪ I am so glad we're pals ♪

14
00:01:57,351 --> 00:02:01,221
♪ Can we pretty
please play a game ♪

15
00:02:01,321 --> 00:02:02,289
♪ Pretty please ♪

16
00:02:02,389 --> 00:02:05,292
♪ Pretty, pretty please ♪

17
00:02:05,392 --> 00:02:09,063
♪ We will have so much fun ♪

18
00:02:09,162 --> 00:02:13,266
♪ Just two pals, having fun ♪

19
00:02:13,367 --> 00:02:16,971
♪ Will you stay
a while with me here ♪

20
00:02:17,071 --> 00:02:19,272
♪ Pretty please ♪

21
00:02:19,373 --> 00:02:22,810
♪ Pretty please ♪

22
00:02:22,910 --> 00:02:26,681
♪ Settle in everyone ♪

23
00:02:26,781 --> 00:02:30,250
♪ Our day's just begun ♪

24
00:02:30,350 --> 00:02:33,153
♪ Pretty please ♪

25
00:02:33,253 --> 00:02:34,922
Thank you, pal.

26
00:02:35,023 --> 00:02:38,826
(soft piano music)

27
00:02:38,926 --> 00:02:40,595
Hello there, pal.

28
00:02:40,895 --> 00:02:42,563
I've been thinking about you.

29
00:02:42,664 --> 00:02:46,199
I've been thinking
a whole lot, in fact.

30
00:02:47,535 --> 00:02:50,104
It's very nice
to finally meet you.

31
00:02:50,203 --> 00:02:52,707
My name is Mr. Jensen,

32
00:02:52,807 --> 00:02:55,943
but my pals call me James.

33
00:02:58,012 --> 00:03:00,548
Oh, I almost forgot.

34
00:03:00,648 --> 00:03:03,851
I found something
I'd like to show you.

35
00:03:04,118 --> 00:03:05,853
Our good pal, Marty Mailbox,

36
00:03:05,953 --> 00:03:08,188
has been keeping it safe for us.

37
00:03:08,690 --> 00:03:11,224
What do you have
for us today, Marty?

38
00:03:13,127 --> 00:03:17,899
Oh boy, I am fond of things
that come in plastic bags.

39
00:03:17,999 --> 00:03:19,399
Let's take a look.

40
00:03:30,477 --> 00:03:34,214
(soft piano music)

41
00:03:35,183 --> 00:03:37,552
All right, here we go.

42
00:03:42,657 --> 00:03:44,726
Have you seen
one of these before?

43
00:03:44,826 --> 00:03:46,060
Well, I bet you have.

44
00:03:46,160 --> 00:03:47,427
You've probably
seen one every time

45
00:03:47,528 --> 00:03:49,964
you step into
Mommy and Daddy's house.

46
00:03:50,965 --> 00:03:52,734
Do you know what this says?

47
00:03:53,801 --> 00:03:58,539
W-E-L-C-O-M-E.

48
00:03:59,339 --> 00:04:01,909
That spells, welcome.

49
00:04:02,009 --> 00:04:03,978
Let's put this where it belongs.

50
00:04:04,078 --> 00:04:05,780
Do you know where that is?

51
00:04:08,149 --> 00:04:09,884
Well here, I'll show you.

52
00:04:14,856 --> 00:04:18,593
It really is pretty out
here today, isn't it?

53
00:04:18,693 --> 00:04:21,629
(dog barking)

54
00:04:29,504 --> 00:04:31,739
Well, here we are.

55
00:04:31,839 --> 00:04:34,742
This is where
the welcome mat goes.

56
00:04:36,210 --> 00:04:39,747
(soft piano music)

57
00:04:45,653 --> 00:04:47,121
Perfect.

58
00:04:47,221 --> 00:04:48,723
Let's go inside.

59
00:04:52,292 --> 00:04:55,763
(soft piano music)

60
00:04:55,863 --> 00:04:57,430
Oh, dear.

61
00:04:58,032 --> 00:05:00,935
It looks like I forgot
the house keys again.

62
00:05:01,035 --> 00:05:02,469
Silly me.

63
00:05:03,571 --> 00:05:06,373
Have you ever
forgotten something before?

64
00:05:06,707 --> 00:05:11,045
Speaking of forgetting, I forgot
the plastic bag over there.

65
00:05:13,114 --> 00:05:14,515
Excuse me.

66
00:05:18,653 --> 00:05:20,888
I wouldn't wanna be a litterbug.

67
00:05:20,988 --> 00:05:24,892
I'm really glad I didn't forget
this plastic bag here today.

68
00:05:26,627 --> 00:05:28,495
Memory is interesting.

69
00:05:28,596 --> 00:05:31,833
In fact, memory is our

70
00:05:31,933 --> 00:05:33,935
concept of the day.

71
00:05:35,603 --> 00:05:37,505
Memories can be anything.

72
00:05:37,605 --> 00:05:39,339
They can be happy,

73
00:05:39,439 --> 00:05:40,274
(light piano music)

74
00:05:40,373 --> 00:05:42,577
sad,
(dark piano music)

75
00:05:42,677 --> 00:05:44,912
angry.
(dramatic piano music)

76
00:05:45,012 --> 00:05:46,614
- Or even gone.

77
00:05:46,714 --> 00:05:49,784
- Look. It's my
best pal, Monkey.

78
00:05:49,884 --> 00:05:51,285
Let's go say hi.

79
00:05:51,418 --> 00:05:52,286
(uptempo piano music)

80
00:05:52,385 --> 00:05:54,387
Good morning, Mr. Monkey.

81
00:05:54,487 --> 00:05:56,524
- Good morning, Jimbo.

82
00:05:56,624 --> 00:06:00,561
- Mr. Monkey, what did you
mean by memories being gone?

83
00:06:00,661 --> 00:06:04,632
- Well, you've
forgotten things, right?

84
00:06:05,166 --> 00:06:06,601
Like, oh,

85
00:06:08,069 --> 00:06:10,137
the plastic bag.

86
00:06:10,238 --> 00:06:11,539
- That's right.

87
00:06:11,639 --> 00:06:14,742
And it's okay to forget the
little things from time to time.

88
00:06:14,842 --> 00:06:18,546
We all do it.
Even grownups, like me.

89
00:06:19,981 --> 00:06:22,449
- But, Jimmy.

90
00:06:22,550 --> 00:06:24,652
- Yes, Mr. Monkey?

91
00:06:24,752 --> 00:06:28,923
- What if
you forget important things?

92
00:06:29,991 --> 00:06:33,127
What if you forget me?

93
00:06:34,328 --> 00:06:36,597
- The warm moments
we've shared together

94
00:06:36,697 --> 00:06:42,036
are far too nice for me to
forget you, my dear Monkey.

95
00:06:42,136 --> 00:06:46,340
- Ah! (laughing)

96
00:06:46,439 --> 00:06:50,745
I'll never
forget you either, Jimbo.

97
00:06:57,151 --> 00:06:59,486
- Oh, what's that?

98
00:06:59,587 --> 00:07:01,055
Another delivery.

99
00:07:01,155 --> 00:07:03,456
- I wonder what it is.

100
00:07:03,557 --> 00:07:05,425
- Excuse me.
- Hm.

101
00:07:07,261 --> 00:07:09,664
Oh, darn.

102
00:07:09,764 --> 00:07:12,300
It seems I miss
the postlady again.

103
00:07:12,400 --> 00:07:14,235
I can't seem to catch her.

104
00:07:14,335 --> 00:07:15,703
She has such a busy schedule

105
00:07:15,803 --> 00:07:17,505
delivering mail
to the whole town.

106
00:07:17,605 --> 00:07:19,407
I never even get
a chance to say hello.

107
00:07:19,507 --> 00:07:21,976
- What's Marty
got for you, Jimbo?

108
00:07:23,544 --> 00:07:26,080
- Well, it looks like
we just got a letter.

109
00:07:28,516 --> 00:07:29,951
That's odd.

110
00:07:31,352 --> 00:07:34,522
Usually a return
address goes here.

111
00:07:34,622 --> 00:07:36,924
A return address
tells you who sent it.

112
00:07:37,024 --> 00:07:40,394
That way, you know where you
can send a little thank you.

113
00:07:40,493 --> 00:07:44,031
(soft piano music)

114
00:07:48,903 --> 00:07:50,638
- What's it say?

115
00:07:50,738 --> 00:07:54,642
(ominous piano music)

116
00:07:58,112 --> 00:07:59,547
- Freak.

117
00:08:00,781 --> 00:08:02,717
All right, who sent this?

118
00:08:03,551 --> 00:08:05,152
Who wrote this?

119
00:08:06,954 --> 00:08:07,822
Why would?

120
00:08:07,922 --> 00:08:10,124
- I wouldn't worry about
that if I were you.

121
00:08:10,224 --> 00:08:13,527
Probably just a silly
little joker. (laughing)

122
00:08:13,627 --> 00:08:15,129
- You're right, Mr. Monkey.

123
00:08:15,229 --> 00:08:17,698
Say, I think it might be time

124
00:08:17,798 --> 00:08:20,768
for our pal here to
visit the playground.

125
00:08:21,369 --> 00:08:23,637
- What a wonderful idea.

126
00:08:23,738 --> 00:08:27,875
I can introduce them to
all the playground pals.

127
00:08:27,975 --> 00:08:29,910
- Don't worry,
pal. This isn't goodbye.

128
00:08:30,011 --> 00:08:33,614
I'll see you real soon.
Have fun with Mr. Monkey.

129
00:08:33,714 --> 00:08:35,282
You can trust him.

130
00:08:35,383 --> 00:08:39,420
- (laughing) This way, pal.

131
00:08:39,520 --> 00:08:43,124
(bright piano music)

132
00:08:46,694 --> 00:08:48,195
♪ Welcome to the playground ♪

133
00:08:48,295 --> 00:08:49,930
♪ Won't you have a look around ♪

134
00:08:50,031 --> 00:08:51,766
♪ Meet some
pals, join the crowd ♪

135
00:08:51,866 --> 00:08:54,335
♪ Strangers
here cannot be found ♪

136
00:08:54,435 --> 00:08:56,704
♪ Did somebody say stranger ♪

137
00:08:56,804 --> 00:08:58,539
♪ I hope I'm not in danger ♪

138
00:08:58,639 --> 00:09:00,641
♪ No need to
fear while I'm around ♪

139
00:09:00,741 --> 00:09:03,344
♪ So stick with us,
you're safe and sound ♪

140
00:09:03,444 --> 00:09:06,414
(uptempo piano music)

141
00:09:06,515 --> 00:09:08,382
♪ Welcome friend,
we're glad you came ♪

142
00:09:08,482 --> 00:09:10,484
♪ You can ignore
me, I'm pretty lame ♪

143
00:09:10,584 --> 00:09:12,386
♪ Don't be glum, beaver dear ♪

144
00:09:12,486 --> 00:09:15,089
♪ At least not
when the friend is near ♪

145
00:09:15,189 --> 00:09:18,527
(uptempo piano music)

146
00:09:18,626 --> 00:09:20,529
♪ I concur, you seem nice ♪

147
00:09:20,628 --> 00:09:22,663
♪ Now listen
here for good advice ♪

148
00:09:22,763 --> 00:09:24,799
♪ A stranger's
trust must be earned ♪

149
00:09:24,899 --> 00:09:28,503
♪ But with us,
don't be concerned ♪

150
00:09:28,602 --> 00:09:31,739
♪ All of us here
at the playground ♪

151
00:09:31,839 --> 00:09:37,244
♪ Want you to know that you
can trust all of us now ♪

152
00:09:39,313 --> 00:09:40,948
- Even Ferret!

153
00:09:44,985 --> 00:09:50,124
♪ Because we're
all best pals for life ♪

154
00:09:53,594 --> 00:09:54,929
- I'm so glad you were able

155
00:09:55,029 --> 00:09:57,731
to join all of
us on the playground.

156
00:09:57,832 --> 00:10:02,036
This here is my best
puppet pal, Fausty Fox.

157
00:10:02,136 --> 00:10:02,970
- Howdy!

158
00:10:03,070 --> 00:10:06,107
- Second only to my best
pal, you. (laughing)

159
00:10:06,207 --> 00:10:08,943
And Jimmy, of course.

160
00:10:09,210 --> 00:10:09,777
- Did I hear my name?

161
00:10:09,877 --> 00:10:11,679
- Whoa whoa whoa whoa.

162
00:10:12,113 --> 00:10:12,947
- What?

163
00:10:13,047 --> 00:10:14,915
- How did you

164
00:10:15,015 --> 00:10:17,051
get here?

165
00:10:17,151 --> 00:10:18,686
- Well, I,

166
00:10:19,086 --> 00:10:21,021
I just wanted to see
my playground pals and-

167
00:10:21,122 --> 00:10:23,858
- [Beaver] Adults aren't
allowed on the playground.

168
00:10:23,958 --> 00:10:27,628
- Yeah, it's
a place for kids to have fun.

169
00:10:27,728 --> 00:10:31,198
- But, Beaver, Bird, Monkey,

170
00:10:31,298 --> 00:10:35,302
you're all my pals and I
wanted to have fun, too.

171
00:10:35,402 --> 00:10:37,506
- It's okay, Mr. Jensen.

172
00:10:37,606 --> 00:10:39,406
You're our pal too.

173
00:10:39,740 --> 00:10:42,544
- He can stay and
play, can't he, Monkey?

174
00:10:42,943 --> 00:10:44,613
- You're right, Fausty.

175
00:10:44,712 --> 00:10:47,148
But that's not my call to make.

176
00:10:47,248 --> 00:10:48,883
- What?

177
00:10:48,983 --> 00:10:50,251
- Hmm,

178
00:10:50,351 --> 00:10:51,752
I, Rory Lion,

179
00:10:51,852 --> 00:10:53,687
king of the jungle gym,

180
00:10:53,787 --> 00:10:56,023
(dramatic piano music)

181
00:10:56,123 --> 00:10:57,158
will allow it.

182
00:10:57,258 --> 00:11:00,562
(pals cheering)

183
00:11:00,961 --> 00:11:03,030
- Thank you, King Rory.

184
00:11:03,130 --> 00:11:04,331
Thanks.

185
00:11:06,133 --> 00:11:09,270
Sometimes
friends say mean things.

186
00:11:10,605 --> 00:11:13,407
Sometimes
friends might exclude you,

187
00:11:14,708 --> 00:11:18,078
and sometimes
you might even feel lonely.

188
00:11:18,513 --> 00:11:22,183
But real friends don't mean
to make you feel that way,

189
00:11:22,483 --> 00:11:25,819
and it's not because they
don't enjoy your company.

190
00:11:25,920 --> 00:11:28,455
They often have
reasons of their own.

191
00:11:29,624 --> 00:11:32,826
I remember when
I was a little boy, I-

192
00:11:39,099 --> 00:11:42,269
- There are so many memories,
it can be hard to keep track.

193
00:11:42,369 --> 00:11:45,906
Would anyone like to share any
special memories they have?

194
00:11:46,874 --> 00:11:49,476
- I remember one
time I saw a butterfly!

195
00:11:49,977 --> 00:11:54,181
- I remember one time I
lost my dam in a flood.

196
00:11:54,815 --> 00:11:56,951
I was so, so sad.

197
00:11:59,486 --> 00:12:02,657
- I remember last week, a
tasty little snack I had.

198
00:12:02,756 --> 00:12:06,227
Oh, juicy, tender, bloody.

199
00:12:06,327 --> 00:12:07,928
- Oh, that sounds
great, your highness.

200
00:12:08,028 --> 00:12:10,164
What about you, Ferret?

201
00:12:13,602 --> 00:12:15,670
I love it! (laughing)

202
00:12:15,769 --> 00:12:18,939
- Do you have any happy
memories Mr. Jensen?

203
00:12:27,716 --> 00:12:29,183
- I,

204
00:12:29,850 --> 00:12:32,786
I, I I don't

205
00:12:33,320 --> 00:12:34,788
know that I,

206
00:12:37,626 --> 00:12:40,160
I have any happy memories

207
00:12:41,696 --> 00:12:43,130
or any,

208
00:12:43,831 --> 00:12:45,533
sad memories or

209
00:12:49,571 --> 00:12:50,938
any at all.

210
00:12:51,038 --> 00:12:52,607
- Someone stole your memories?

211
00:12:52,707 --> 00:12:54,408
- Oh, no.

212
00:12:54,775 --> 00:12:57,444
- [Fausty] What are we
gonna do, Mr. Jensen?

213
00:12:58,012 --> 00:13:01,248
- Oh, no, no, no, no, no,
no, no, no, no, no, no, no.

214
00:13:01,348 --> 00:13:02,783
Don't go.

215
00:13:02,883 --> 00:13:04,818
It's okay.

216
00:13:05,252 --> 00:13:07,121
We'll, we'll, we'll think
of something, right?

217
00:13:07,221 --> 00:13:08,422
We always do.

218
00:13:08,523 --> 00:13:09,990
- Don't worry, Jimothee.

219
00:13:10,090 --> 00:13:11,825
(dramatic piano music)

220
00:13:11,925 --> 00:13:14,028
Detective Monkey is on the case.

221
00:13:14,128 --> 00:13:17,031
- Woo, he always
gets to the bottom of it.

222
00:13:17,131 --> 00:13:19,900
- Elementary, my dear Fox.

223
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:23,971
- Well, lead the way,
Mr., uh Detective Monkey.

224
00:13:24,071 --> 00:13:27,374
- First thing is first, we
need to examine the body.

225
00:13:28,677 --> 00:13:31,312
I mean, Jim, (laughing)

226
00:13:31,412 --> 00:13:32,846
have a seat.

227
00:13:34,683 --> 00:13:36,450
- If you say so, Detective.

228
00:13:37,851 --> 00:13:40,921
- Okay, let's have a look.

229
00:13:41,790 --> 00:13:43,457
Hmm.

230
00:13:43,558 --> 00:13:45,059
Open, please.

231
00:13:47,729 --> 00:13:50,130
Ah, come on, wider Jimbo.

232
00:13:50,230 --> 00:13:50,998
- Ah, ah.

233
00:13:51,098 --> 00:13:54,902
(tense piano music)

234
00:13:55,670 --> 00:13:58,272
- Taste buds looking normal.

235
00:13:58,606 --> 00:14:02,276
Yes. Perfectly operational jaw.

236
00:14:02,876 --> 00:14:06,046
- Hmm.

237
00:14:06,146 --> 00:14:08,215
- Shh, I'm investigating.

238
00:14:09,350 --> 00:14:12,453
I need to see
those peepers, Jimbo.

239
00:14:12,554 --> 00:14:15,356
Ah, (sniffing).

240
00:14:15,456 --> 00:14:17,525
Irises, pupils, veins.

241
00:14:17,625 --> 00:14:18,827
(tense piano music)

242
00:14:18,926 --> 00:14:19,694
You get all this?

243
00:14:19,794 --> 00:14:21,763
- Yeah, yeah, I got it. Uh huh.

244
00:14:21,862 --> 00:14:23,464
- Okay, good.

245
00:14:23,565 --> 00:14:25,966
- Well, that's good to hear.

246
00:14:26,066 --> 00:14:28,135
- Ah, ah, ah, ah.

247
00:14:29,537 --> 00:14:31,338
Hmm.

248
00:14:31,438 --> 00:14:33,508
Legs long as ever.

249
00:14:33,608 --> 00:14:34,509
- Long as ever.

250
00:14:34,609 --> 00:14:38,278
- Have they had any
trouble wiggling recently?

251
00:14:42,216 --> 00:14:44,485
Just as
I suspected, made of skin.

252
00:14:44,586 --> 00:14:46,086
- Ah, skin.

253
00:14:46,186 --> 00:14:49,323
- Raise your arms now.

254
00:14:49,423 --> 00:14:50,525
Arms operational,

255
00:14:50,625 --> 00:14:52,761
(tense piano music)

256
00:14:52,861 --> 00:14:54,529
and.

257
00:14:54,895 --> 00:14:59,032
(James and Monkey laughing)

258
00:14:59,133 --> 00:15:02,670
(bright piano music)

259
00:15:03,772 --> 00:15:08,075
(James and Monkey laughing)

260
00:15:14,716 --> 00:15:17,251
- Wow.

261
00:15:17,351 --> 00:15:18,520
That was fun.

262
00:15:20,354 --> 00:15:22,657
Did you enjoy
that as much as I did?

263
00:15:24,425 --> 00:15:27,294
- All right,
I've solved the case.

264
00:15:27,394 --> 00:15:28,929
(dramatic piano music)
- You have?

265
00:15:29,029 --> 00:15:30,598
- The answer is,

266
00:15:35,369 --> 00:15:36,905
Profoctopus
