No?

537
00:33:47,996 --> 00:33:50,163
Do you have an idea?

538
00:33:51,633 --> 00:33:53,333
Well, tell us.

539
00:33:55,469 --> 00:33:58,506
It's a surprise.

540
00:33:59,206 --> 00:34:02,242
Well, I'm open to any ideas
that might cheer me up.

541
00:34:04,779 --> 00:34:06,213
Marty,

542
00:34:06,781 --> 00:34:08,516
you found my music.

543
00:34:11,920 --> 00:34:15,389
(rhythmic tapping)

544
00:34:23,865 --> 00:34:28,068
(sucking on empty container)

545
00:34:28,168 --> 00:34:32,406
(light instrumental music)

546
00:34:48,957 --> 00:34:51,325
May I have this dance?

547
00:34:51,425 --> 00:34:55,663
(light instrumental music)

548
00:35:04,072 --> 00:35:05,773
- Come on Playhouse.

549
00:35:05,873 --> 00:35:07,642
Yeah, you can do it.

550
00:35:08,009 --> 00:35:12,212
(light instrumental music)

551
00:35:21,956 --> 00:35:23,725
Now everybody.

552
00:35:23,992 --> 00:35:28,395
(good time instrumental music)

553
00:35:44,012 --> 00:35:46,179
(good time music continues)

554
00:35:46,279 --> 00:35:49,651
(James laughing)

555
00:36:00,728 --> 00:36:02,162
- Fellas?

556
00:36:02,830 --> 00:36:04,197
Where'd you go?

557
00:36:08,569 --> 00:36:10,505
Oh, did you say something?

558
00:36:11,506 --> 00:36:15,208
I didn't realize,
the post lady is here?

559
00:36:16,911 --> 00:36:18,680
Oh no, did I miss her again?

560
00:36:18,780 --> 00:36:20,213
Oh, Mrs. Post lady?

561
00:36:20,313 --> 00:36:21,248
- [Post Lady] I'm sorry.

562
00:36:21,348 --> 00:36:22,583
- Oh, I'm so glad
I finally caught you.

563
00:36:22,684 --> 00:36:23,651
- I have a busy schedule...
- I wanted to send-

564
00:36:23,751 --> 00:36:25,520
- ...delivering
mail to the whole town.

565
00:36:25,620 --> 00:36:27,155
- Huh?

566
00:36:27,254 --> 00:36:30,124
- I'm sorry,
sir. I really must be off.

567
00:36:30,223 --> 00:36:32,325
(jazz piano music)

568
00:36:32,426 --> 00:36:34,327
You smell the same.

569
00:36:35,262 --> 00:36:38,099
I used to call
it the smelly stuff.

570
00:36:38,465 --> 00:36:39,734
- [Post Lady] I don't know
what you're talking about.

571
00:36:39,834 --> 00:36:41,268
- Mom.

572
00:36:42,870 --> 00:36:45,039
I used to watch you
put it on every morning

573
00:36:45,139 --> 00:36:47,642
when you were
getting ready for work.

574
00:36:47,942 --> 00:36:51,112
Once, I found the bottle

575
00:36:51,478 --> 00:36:53,346
and no one was around.

576
00:36:55,083 --> 00:36:57,719
I put it on just to be like you.

577
00:36:57,819 --> 00:36:58,886
(jazz piano music)

578
00:36:58,986 --> 00:37:00,420
But,

579
00:37:02,824 --> 00:37:04,424
I put on too much,

580
00:37:04,525 --> 00:37:07,128
and it got in my eyes.

581
00:37:07,528 --> 00:37:10,363
That shit
really stung really bad.

582
00:37:11,199 --> 00:37:12,332
And dad walked in.

583
00:37:12,432 --> 00:37:13,868
Sir, if I don't leave now,

584
00:37:13,968 --> 00:37:17,471
the next house will never
get its mail on time.

585
00:37:17,839 --> 00:37:19,040
- Oh, oh no. Don't go.

586
00:37:19,140 --> 00:37:22,143
Come, come dance with us.

587
00:37:22,242 --> 00:37:23,010
Come dance with us, mom.

588
00:37:23,111 --> 00:37:24,879
- Have a good afternoon.

589
00:37:40,962 --> 00:37:42,362
- What do I do?

590
00:37:47,367 --> 00:37:49,103
Great idea.

591
00:37:49,203 --> 00:37:50,605
Thank you, pal.

592
00:37:55,342 --> 00:38:00,014
(light commotion
in the playhouse)

593
00:38:04,284 --> 00:38:07,655
(even breathing)

594
00:38:15,763 --> 00:38:19,133
(Monkey giggling)

595
00:38:19,466 --> 00:38:21,903
(soft piano music)

596
00:38:22,003 --> 00:38:23,871
Do you build traps often?

597
00:38:26,040 --> 00:38:29,043
People trap all sorts of things.

598
00:38:29,544 --> 00:38:33,014
They trap mice to
keep their homes clean.

599
00:38:33,848 --> 00:38:36,551
They trap
bigger animals for food

600
00:38:36,651 --> 00:38:40,922
or to make nice clothes
with their furs and skins.

601
00:38:43,024 --> 00:38:47,028
People even trap parents.

602
00:38:47,360 --> 00:38:50,898
(soft piano music)

603
00:38:55,102 --> 00:38:56,604
Now,

604
00:38:56,704 --> 00:38:57,939
the bait.

605
00:38:59,907 --> 00:39:03,010
(ominous music)

606
00:39:06,346 --> 00:39:07,414
(Monkey grunting)

607
00:39:07,515 --> 00:39:09,116
What do you think, Marty?

608
00:39:10,985 --> 00:39:11,853
Oh, you're right.

609
00:39:11,953 --> 00:39:14,454
I did forget to
see what mom sent me.

610
00:39:17,625 --> 00:39:21,361
(eerie piano music)

611
00:39:38,079 --> 00:39:41,849
(eerie music continues)

612
00:39:47,487 --> 00:39:50,591
(dark music)

613
00:39:52,994 --> 00:39:56,163
(dark rumblings)

614
00:40:01,569 --> 00:40:04,538
I didn't see you there, pal.

615
00:40:05,840 --> 00:40:08,475
I have bad news.

616
00:40:09,610 --> 00:40:13,681
I'm remembering
all kinds of things now.

617
00:40:14,447 --> 00:40:15,850
Like,

618
00:40:16,517 --> 00:40:17,919
how to cook,

619
00:40:25,326 --> 00:40:28,663
or at least how
I was taught to cook.

620
00:40:29,397 --> 00:40:30,831
I don't

621
00:40:32,133 --> 00:40:33,401
quite remember who,

622
00:40:33,500 --> 00:40:36,837
but someone must have taught me.

623
00:40:44,477 --> 00:40:48,115
I wonder if this cow had a mom.

624
00:40:51,419 --> 00:40:52,887
I wonder

625
00:40:54,522 --> 00:40:58,426
if they played in
the pastures together.

626
00:40:58,926 --> 00:41:01,562
It's not like
they had much else to do.

627
00:41:09,870 --> 00:41:12,073
Do you know what a cigarette is?

628
00:41:13,341 --> 00:41:17,878
My mom loved cigarettes.

629
00:41:18,946 --> 00:41:22,049
She went out to buy a pack once,

630
00:41:22,149 --> 00:41:25,686
and when she came back
home, the house was on fire.

631
00:41:25,786 --> 00:41:30,257
(dark instrumental music)

632
00:41:30,591 --> 00:41:34,795
I wonder if this cow's
mom smokes cigarettes?

633
00:41:36,097 --> 00:41:38,165
Does yours? I hope not.

634
00:41:39,934 --> 00:41:42,870
(dark music)

635
00:41:46,474 --> 00:41:48,776
I've made a mistake.

636
00:41:49,210 --> 00:41:52,513
And what do we do
when we make a mistake?

637
00:41:52,613 --> 00:41:56,717
We say we're sorry and we
try our best next time.

638
00:42:00,321 --> 00:42:03,257
I'm sorry, hand.

639
00:42:15,903 --> 00:42:18,639
This is gonna
need a big bandaid.

640
00:42:28,549 --> 00:42:30,084
Maybe I should take
some of the food we made

641
00:42:30,184 --> 00:42:31,952
to the playground pals.

642
00:42:33,154 --> 00:42:35,256
Wrap my hand,

643
00:42:35,990 --> 00:42:37,324
if I

644
00:42:37,425 --> 00:42:38,826
get it.

645
00:42:42,363 --> 00:42:45,966
True pals are never apart,

646
00:42:47,435 --> 00:42:49,203
maybe in distance,

647
00:42:49,804 --> 00:42:51,072
but never in heart.

648
00:42:51,172 --> 00:42:53,874
- [Bird] Don't
worry, that's why I'm here.

649
00:42:54,575 --> 00:42:55,576
- Bird.

650
00:42:55,676 --> 00:42:58,412
- That's right.
I'm here to help.

651
00:42:58,513 --> 00:42:59,580
- Oh, that's good.

652
00:42:59,680 --> 00:43:03,017
I could really use some
help getting cheered up.

653
00:43:03,117 --> 00:43:06,987
- Oh, I see. A bad case
of the blues got you down?

654
00:43:07,888 --> 00:43:10,191
Well, there's
only one place to go.

655
00:43:10,291 --> 00:43:11,526
- Where's that bird?

656
00:43:11,625 --> 00:43:14,228
- Six feet deep
with maggots in your eyes.

657
00:43:15,863 --> 00:43:16,630
- What?
- A pile of flesh

658
00:43:16,730 --> 00:43:18,732
to feed the worms.

659
00:43:20,468 --> 00:43:23,871
♪ Early bird gets the worm ♪

660
00:43:23,971 --> 00:43:25,673
- Bird, you're scaring me.

661
00:43:25,773 --> 00:43:27,274
- Oh, don't be a downer.

662
00:43:27,374 --> 00:43:29,376
That's Beaver's job. Bye.

663
00:43:31,846 --> 00:43:35,116
- Well, it's
a bad thing I'm here too.

664
00:43:35,584 --> 00:43:40,988
After all, you're
just so, so sad today.

665
00:43:41,088 --> 00:43:42,790
- Any more tears
and he might just snap.

666
00:43:42,890 --> 00:43:44,692
Oh, poor Mr. Jensen.

667
00:43:44,792 --> 00:43:46,861
- Poor Mr. Jensen.

668
00:43:46,961 --> 00:43:50,498
He might even be
happier as bird food.

669
00:43:50,599 --> 00:43:53,267
- Early bird gets the worm.

670
00:43:53,901 --> 00:43:54,668
- That's not funny.

671
00:43:54,768 --> 00:43:57,471
- Come on, Mr. Jensen.

672
00:43:57,572 --> 00:44:00,174
Where's your sense of humor?

673
00:44:00,274 --> 00:44:03,512
(Bird laughing)

674
00:44:03,612 --> 00:44:06,013
(Beaver laughing)
- Why are you laughing?

675
00:44:06,113 --> 00:44:07,114
Stop laughing.

676
00:44:07,214 --> 00:44:09,250
(both laughing)

677
00:44:09,350 --> 00:44:10,751
Shut up!

678
00:44:13,954 --> 00:44:16,490
- You said a bad word.

679
00:44:16,591 --> 00:44:22,062
♪ Shut up, shut
up, shut up (laughing) ♪

680
00:44:22,163 --> 00:44:24,198
(both laughing)

681
00:44:24,298 --> 00:44:26,300
- Shut up! Shut up!

682
00:44:27,168 --> 00:44:28,068
Shut up.

683
00:44:28,169 --> 00:44:30,671
Shut up, shut up, shut
up, shut up, shut up,

684
00:44:30,771 --> 00:44:33,374
shut up, shut up, shut up.

685
00:44:35,610 --> 00:44:38,245
Shut up, shut up, shut up.

686
00:44:39,581 --> 00:44:42,850
(pals laughing)

687
00:44:51,560 --> 00:44:54,895
(Bird squealing)

688
00:45:01,168 --> 00:45:04,371
(James screaming)

689
00:45:04,905 --> 00:45:08,209
(James gasping)

690
00:45:11,278 --> 00:45:12,146
What do I do?

691
00:45:12,246 --> 00:45:15,382
(pals squealing)

692
00:45:17,686 --> 00:45:20,387
No, no, no.
I don't wanna do that.

693
00:45:20,721 --> 00:45:22,423
Pals don't hurt pals.

694
00:45:24,593 --> 00:45:27,161
But, but I don't want to.

695
00:45:31,232 --> 00:45:34,368
(ominous music)

696
00:45:39,340 --> 00:45:40,975
You're right.

697
00:45:41,710 --> 00:45:43,177
Thanks pal.

698
00:45:46,514 --> 00:45:49,917
(pals whimpering)

699
00:45:56,625 --> 00:45:59,260
(opening door)

700
00:45:59,360 --> 00:46:02,496
(ominous music)

701
00:46:03,230 --> 00:46:04,865
Are you sure?

702
00:46:08,603 --> 00:46:09,770
Okay.

703
00:46:09,870 --> 00:46:12,674
(ominous music)

704
00:46:12,773 --> 00:46:16,010
(door creaking)

705
00:46:48,075 --> 00:46:52,479
- James, please don't.

706
00:46:52,580 --> 00:46:54,815
- [Beaver] We're your pals.

707
00:46:54,915 --> 00:46:56,884
(Bird whimpering)

708
00:46:56,984 --> 00:46:59,721
- Pretty please James!
- James!

709
00:46:59,820 --> 00:47:01,690
Pretty please!

710
00:47:01,790 --> 00:47:03,257
Pretty please!

711
00:47:03,357 --> 00:47:04,425
- [Bird] Please!

712
00:47:06,393 --> 00:47:07,729
(Beaver sobbing)

713
00:47:07,828 --> 00:47:11,065
(tamping dirt)

714
00:47:11,599 --> 00:47:15,135
(soft piano music)

715
00:47:22,476 --> 00:47:24,512
- What you doing Jimbo?

716
00:47:24,612 --> 00:47:27,448
(bright piano music)

717
00:47:27,549 --> 00:47:28,982
Pal.

718
00:47:31,385 --> 00:47:36,490
You look like you've lost
your bananas. (laughing)

719
00:47:37,692 --> 00:47:39,126
- No, no.

720
00:47:40,861 --> 00:47:42,363
I'm doing swell.

721
00:47:42,463 --> 00:47:45,399
- Oh, glad to hear it.

722
00:47:45,499 --> 00:47:49,136
(eerie piano music)

723
00:47:49,236 --> 00:47:53,073
- Monkey, how did
you get over the fence?

724
00:47:53,173 --> 00:47:56,110
- Ah, I have my way.

725
00:47:56,845 --> 00:47:58,513
Hey,

726
00:47:58,613 --> 00:48:00,447
what's that for?

727
00:48:03,150 --> 00:48:05,185
- Just some cleaning.

728
00:48:05,820 --> 00:48:07,254
Someone

729
00:48:08,021 --> 00:48:11,559
took out a shovel out earlier.

730
00:48:11,659 --> 00:48:14,027
- Ah, peculiar.

731
00:48:14,128 --> 00:48:17,965
I don't seem to remember
anyone else being here.

732
00:48:19,466 --> 00:48:20,901
Do you?

733
00:48:22,537 --> 00:48:23,370
- I thought I was the one

734
00:48:23,470 --> 00:48:26,173
with the missing
memory, silly Monkey.

735
00:48:27,509 --> 00:48:28,810
It's just us,

736
00:48:28,909 --> 00:48:30,277
me and my pal.

737
00:48:30,377 --> 00:48:34,516
Gardening,
we planted that flower.

738
00:48:34,616 --> 00:48:38,185
(eerie piano music)

739
00:48:43,591 --> 00:48:47,829
- You know,
I've always loved the smell

740
00:48:47,928 --> 00:48:49,564
of fresh dirt.

741
00:48:50,998 --> 00:48:54,301
- Why are
you here anyway, Monkey?

742
00:48:55,637 --> 00:48:57,171
- Oh, that's right.

743
00:48:57,271 --> 00:49:00,608
I originally came to
give you some good news.

744
00:49:00,708 --> 00:49:01,709
- Oh.

745
00:49:01,810 --> 00:49:04,779
- We have a lead on your
stolen memories. (laughing)

746
00:49:04,879 --> 00:49:06,246
- Oh.

747
00:49:06,346 --> 00:49:08,850
- That, that is good news.

748
00:49:09,517 --> 00:49:12,854
- Oh, well, why don't you
come back to the playground

749
00:49:12,953 --> 00:49:15,022
and see all the pals?

750
00:49:16,691 --> 00:49:18,459
You should come, too.

751
00:49:19,359 --> 00:49:21,094
We miss you.

752
00:49:21,195 --> 00:49:24,965
(eerie piano music)

753
00:49:39,213 --> 00:49:43,785
This way. (laughing)

754
00:49:43,885 --> 00:49:47,120
(ominous music)

755
00:49:50,190 --> 00:49:53,628
(ominous rumbling)

756
00:49:58,999 --> 00:50:00,768
- What happened?

757
00:50:03,470 --> 00:50:05,105
What happened?

758
00:50:07,709 --> 00:50:09,243
(someone screaming)

759
00:50:09,343 --> 00:50:10,578
Oh, oh.

760
00:50:11,913 --> 00:50:14,248
Fausty? Are you okay?

761
00:50:15,382 --> 00:50:17,719
- Mr. Jensen? Who did this?

762
00:50:17,819 --> 00:50:19,654
- [Profoctopus]
Who do you think?

763
00:50:19,754 --> 00:50:22,724
(dark music)

764
00:50:24,124 --> 00:50:25,560
- I don't remember.

765
00:50:25,660 --> 00:50:27,962
- Who else, but the Freak.

766
00:50:28,061 --> 00:50:30,063
And it's not done yet.

767
00:50:30,163 --> 00:50:32,934
It won't rest until we're all

768
00:50:33,033 --> 00:50:36,938
as miserable as
it is. (laughing)

769
00:50:37,037 --> 00:50:38,338
- You were
supposed to protect us.

770
00:50:39,607 --> 00:50:41,341
Where were you?

771
00:50:43,011 --> 00:50:44,411
- No.

772
00:50:45,045 --> 00:50:47,015
No. It wasn't my job.

773
00:50:47,114 --> 00:50:49,617
It isn't my
job, it's King Rory's.

774
00:50:50,952 --> 00:50:52,654
It's King Rory's.

775
00:50:52,754 --> 00:50:53,588
King Rory.

776
00:50:53,688 --> 00:50:55,590
King Rory, come quick.

777
00:50:55,690 --> 00:50:57,525
The playground, it's-

778
00:50:57,625 --> 00:50:58,993
- Oh, I am aware.

779
00:50:59,092 --> 00:51:03,831
I, King Rory,
protector of the playground

780
00:51:03,932 --> 00:51:06,333
see all.

781
00:51:06,801 --> 00:51:08,703
- Then why didn't you stop it?

782
00:51:09,938 --> 00:51:12,874
- I know what you did.

783
00:51:13,173 --> 00:51:14,509
- I didn't do this.

784
00:51:14,609 --> 00:51:16,711
- Not the fire.

785
00:51:17,545 --> 00:51:18,746
(chime ringing)

786
00:51:18,846 --> 00:51:20,615
- Beaver, Bird, they're,
they're, they're fine. They're-

787
00:51:20,715 --> 00:51:22,115
- James!

788
00:51:23,150 --> 00:51:26,721
I know everything.
(chime ringing)

789
00:51:26,821 --> 00:51:28,255
- Everything?

790
00:51:30,592 --> 00:51:31,993
(Rory grunting)

791
00:51:32,092 --> 00:51:35,095
I won't let
you ruin this for me.

792
00:51:35,195 --> 00:51:37,164
- Please, don't.

793
00:51:39,366 --> 00:51:42,202
- You should've
stopped the fire.

794
00:51:42,302 --> 00:51:44,939
You should have
stopped the fire!

795
00:51:45,039 --> 00:51:47,107
(Rory whimpering)

796
00:51:47,207 --> 00:51:50,444
(Rory grunting)

797
00:51:52,580 --> 00:51:55,717
(James grunting)

798
00:51:58,318 --> 00:52:02,557
(James yelling and crying)

799
00:52:10,698 --> 00:52:13,400
- How's
it hanging, Jungle Jimbo?

800
00:52:15,036 --> 00:52:17,038
- Monkey, I'm so sorry.

801
00:52:17,137 --> 00:52:22,010
- For what? (laughing)

802
00:52:22,110 --> 00:52:23,544
- I,

803
00:52:24,112 --> 00:52:25,546
I did it.

804
00:52:27,147 --> 00:52:28,750
I killed Bird

805
00:52:32,587 --> 00:52:33,821
and Beaver

806
00:52:35,857 --> 00:52:36,958
and King Rory.

807
00:52:37,058 --> 00:52:38,492
- Rory?

808
00:52:42,063 --> 00:52:44,666
- Our pal, King Rory.

809
00:52:45,033 --> 00:52:47,902
- [Monkey]
That didn't ring a bell.

810
00:52:48,002 --> 00:52:49,504
(chime ringing)

811
00:52:49,604 --> 00:52:51,371
(wind blowing)

812
